From: Danylo Storozhev <daniel.storozhev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 12:54:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] leds: lp5562: initialize LED to amber at boot

Light the amber channel during driver probe so the rider sees boot
progress; userland switches it to green when boot completes.

Folds the original 5.4 green-at-boot hack and the later
amber-at-boot revision (Teal Bauer) into one patch.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific]
---
 drivers/leds/leds-lp5562.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/leds/leds-lp5562.c b/drivers/leds/leds-lp5562.c
index b26bcc81d..9cee50032 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/leds-lp5562.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/leds-lp5562.c
@@ -149,10 +149,10 @@ static int lp5562_post_init_device(struct lp55xx_chip *chip)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	/* Initialize all channels PWM to zero -> leds off */
+	/* Initialize LED to amber at boot; userland sets green when ready */
 	lp55xx_write(chip, LP5562_REG_R_PWM, 0);
 	lp55xx_write(chip, LP5562_REG_G_PWM, 0);
-	lp55xx_write(chip, LP5562_REG_B_PWM, 0);
+	lp55xx_write(chip, LP5562_REG_B_PWM, 255);
 	lp55xx_write(chip, LP5562_REG_W_PWM, 0);
 
 	/* Set LED map as register PWM by default */
-- 
